1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,540
How do you feel like tourism at this point is either helping or hurting the Caribbean?

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:07,420
Yeah, I think we have an over-dependency on it.

3
00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:08,740
And COVID taught us that.

4
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:15,400
And, you know, looking at how we are willing to risk our own health to accommodate tourists, because that is our bread and butter.

5
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:18,220
I think that was very illuminating for us.

6
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:24,040
And yes, we even though we still have this connection to the land, I still think that we are having this first world disconnect.

7
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:25,520
Because, of course, now we're on Instagram.

8
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:29,580
I'm seeing so-and-so is enjoying themselves and is popping this and that.

9
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:30,780
And me going to work the land?

10
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:35,820
Me, I want to go and work in a nice office job and thing or manage like a nice hotel and whatever.

11
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:38,320
So a lot of us are disconnecting from the land.

12
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:48,180
Our food import bill and then, you know, having to accommodate these foreign tastes because of tourists, they want strawberries and they want continental breakfast and they want this or whatever.

13
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:52,400
And then it's like, it is, it is to me a huge detriment.

14
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:55,520
And I think if we don't do it properly, there's a way to keep a balance.

